        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "79900518-7a45-369e-9190-1441694d90de",
                "word": "zigomar",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "7777b101-ff6a-4c75-8f88-ceeb5bc5feeb",
                        "entry_id": "79900518-7a45-369e-9190-1441694d90de",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "zigomars"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "bd4f626d-0996-4668-8a1b-b65877d2facd",
                        "entry_id": "79900518-7a45-369e-9190-1441694d90de",
                        "tags": [
                            "Moins courant"
                        ],
                        "form": "zigomard"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7a31c65c-f6ca-39f6-a52b-b4381c79764a",
                        "entry_id": "79900518-7a45-369e-9190-1441694d90de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Zigoto, individu bizarre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "familiar",
                            "pejorative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39291943-db51-4b0b-986e-e6e21a0b83ea",
                                "sense_id": "7a31c65c-f6ca-39f6-a52b-b4381c79764a",
                                "text": "Il m’énerve, le gars ! Il insinue quoi ? Que j’ai des frangins malgré moi ? Que j’ignore tout de ma famille ? Que je suis un zigomar ?",
                                "translation": "Je suis pas un zigomar, je beugle. — (Caroline Guézille, Préhi-story, page 147, 2010, Publibook/Société des écrivains)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e65cf58b-85a2-4b78-a2c8-db77e444da89",
                                "sense_id": "7a31c65c-f6ca-39f6-a52b-b4381c79764a",
                                "text": "Inévitablement, je dirais même, naturellement, il arrive un point où tu es de plus en plus consciente et lucide de l’impasse qu’est ton programme de pensée, et alors si à ce moment-là tu rencontres un zigomar comme moi qui bat tout en brèche… […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25131a29-66dd-406b-9eaa-59d9ee4f9740",
                                "sense_id": "7a31c65c-f6ca-39f6-a52b-b4381c79764a",
                                "text": "Oui, même que j’y mets de la bonne volonté, de m’accorder avec un zigomar qui me laisse boire le canon sans me tenir compagnie !"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "53bc2450-0add-39c8-b98f-9603d114eed4",
                        "entry_id": "79900518-7a45-369e-9190-1441694d90de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Surnom donné au sabre de cavalerie au cours de la Grande Guerre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "figuratively",
                            "slang"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bf98829-cd6f-4da5-879a-751aae92dc99",
                                "sense_id": "53bc2450-0add-39c8-b98f-9603d114eed4",
                                "text": "Le sabre s’appelait désormais Zigomar et l’obusier de tranchée, Crapouillot. La baïonnette se prénommait joliment Rosalie. Toutes ces appellations seront aussitôt reprises dans les discussions des tacticiens de l’arrière […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "88a6e1f7-f653-32a5-a624-516d7f5e95c2",
                        "entry_id": "79900518-7a45-369e-9190-1441694d90de",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pénis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "familiar",
                            "figuratively",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3aaa114a-1657-418e-a5d4-acda0882f21b",
                                "sense_id": "88a6e1f7-f653-32a5-a624-516d7f5e95c2",
                                "text": "Et une fois sur le lit, le biotropisme fondamental de mon zigomar s’alliant à la nutation de l’axe médian de l’œillet de ma belle fait qu’on y retourne, pour un tour."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f999a4b5-0f9d-4c5d-b1e0-f9d48cdbd558",
                                "sense_id": "88a6e1f7-f653-32a5-a624-516d7f5e95c2",
                                "text": "Et puis tout d’un coup, il m’a attrapé, m’a poussé dans l’herbe et m’a badigeonné le bas-ventre et tout ce qu’il y a en dessous (du zigomar aux boules) du contenu d’un yaourt que nous n’avions pas mangé."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a2fc7bf5-861a-4a05-a918-3c2c59c60b50",
                        "source_entry_id": "79900518-7a45-369e-9190-1441694d90de",
                        "source_sense_id": "7a31c65c-f6ca-39f6-a52b-b4381c79764a",
                        "source_sense_description": "Zigoto, individu bizarre",
                        "target_lang_word": "guy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "guy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab290ec8-76da-3840-b02d-069dbfccb5da",
                                        "entry_id": "e4211b83-90f4-3bc7-a1d6-7a507d2bc35d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An effigy of a man burned on a bonfire on the anniversary of the Gunpowder Plot (5th November)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a88358ec-8339-391a-833e-dec05b225c03",
                                        "entry_id": "e4211b83-90f4-3bc7-a1d6-7a507d2bc35d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person of eccentric appearance or dress; a \\\"fright\\\"."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "066a49c0-f62a-4938-bd16-f778d9b24b17",
                                                "sense_id": "a88358ec-8339-391a-833e-dec05b225c03",
                                                "text": "“But shan’t I look a guy?”\n“Not a bit of it. Jist the very kick!”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dc17055-c6b8-4dd1-be43-ef3c8c316b3c",
                                                "sense_id": "a88358ec-8339-391a-833e-dec05b225c03",
                                                "text": "I am always a perfect guy, whatever I wear, when I sit against a red curtain. You men say that a woman always knows when she’s good-looking, but I am happy to say I know when I look a guy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a03bbcd5-fad9-410d-8608-75c1ee099974",
                                                "sense_id": "a88358ec-8339-391a-833e-dec05b225c03",
                                                "text": "And the lady from the provinces, who dresses like a guy,\nAnd who “doesn’t think she dances, but would rather like to try” […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86f3ad88-b2c8-48fd-b2e8-cd90137f6bd8",
                                                "sense_id": "a88358ec-8339-391a-833e-dec05b225c03",
                                                "text": "Why are you so ashamed that her child saw you looking a guy, sprawled on the floor, spilling cakes?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dacdf568-e29a-3668-b430-c2a99adcad25",
                                        "entry_id": "e4211b83-90f4-3bc7-a1d6-7a507d2bc35d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man or boy; a fellow."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79d6ac00-8ab1-4d3b-b314-da799fdb7cc3",
                                                "sense_id": "dacdf568-e29a-3668-b430-c2a99adcad25",
                                                "text": "“You don't say so? I thought he was some guy from Pennsylvania.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42c9c377-0080-47f5-b79b-a96debe97132",
                                                "sense_id": "dacdf568-e29a-3668-b430-c2a99adcad25",
                                                "text": "\"Hi, guys. Did you have a fun time at school?\" said Katherine.\n\"Yeah we did,\" said Stacy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80d56d51-7103-4fae-a6ba-e7519bc7a9bb",
                                                "sense_id": "dacdf568-e29a-3668-b430-c2a99adcad25",
                                                "text": "She was one of the guys, but they were also very much aware that she was an attractive young woman."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "738b8185-0561-4f04-b77d-ee06393c487e",
                                                "sense_id": "dacdf568-e29a-3668-b430-c2a99adcad25",
                                                "text": "Let’s be honest. “Have I kissed too many guys?” is not a question that mature, sexually active women are likely to be asking Google."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1ed74e7b-05dd-315c-ac50-1df201f72b58",
                                        "entry_id": "e4211b83-90f4-3bc7-a1d6-7a507d2bc35d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person (see usage notes)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "especially",
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9e55675-d4e7-4888-b6a6-446fd47c8de4",
                                                "sense_id": "1ed74e7b-05dd-315c-ac50-1df201f72b58",
                                                "text": "My “Guys” actually constitute a collection of people that range from my nearest and dearest girlfriends, my immediate and extended family, co-workers and acquaintances that care."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f002bdc7-0042-4c1c-9698-bfa5a815e836",
                                                "sense_id": "1ed74e7b-05dd-315c-ac50-1df201f72b58",
                                                "text": "My “guys,” as I call the group, are loving and hilarious, serious and the epitome of love. They are both male and female in their presence and have never had the experience of inhabiting a physical body—they are beings of light."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb00a3af-b45d-42ed-87f1-59670bc212c5",
                                                "sense_id": "1ed74e7b-05dd-315c-ac50-1df201f72b58",
                                                "text": "I recently rewatched the original Star Wars trilogy. I'm not a Star Wars guy, but I did enjoy them a lot more than I did the first time. / The movie seemed more like just Ellie's personal journey into being, like, \"Wow, religion can be cool, I guess\", which is fine, but I'm more of a sci-fi guy, so I would rather read the book."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a063669e-4ef7-3f92-879f-5b4e659af3b7",
                                        "entry_id": "e4211b83-90f4-3bc7-a1d6-7a507d2bc35d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything seen to have character and personality, such as an animal or a toy."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac56af4c-4f93-4d77-8d4a-c9cc4b01c7dc",
                                                "sense_id": "a063669e-4ef7-3f92-879f-5b4e659af3b7",
                                                "text": "The dog's left foreleg was broken, poor little guy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7041f97-3ee2-4daa-8a67-d858953b71a6",
                                                "sense_id": "a063669e-4ef7-3f92-879f-5b4e659af3b7",
                                                "text": "I just want to play with my guys. My guys are my friends, they're stuffed animals or little action figures I have a lot of them."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7555d91d-2492-3015-bbe1-aa7b58981116",
                                        "entry_id": "e4211b83-90f4-3bc7-a1d6-7a507d2bc35d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Buster, Mack, fella, bud, man."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "term-of-address"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5f8e99fb-ec3b-4073-b03b-220f4776d492",
                                                "sense_id": "7555d91d-2492-3015-bbe1-aa7b58981116",
                                                "text": "Hey, guy, give a man a break, would ya?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "03fc7a54-b72b-3bbf-bbbe-568d9f8581e2",
                                        "entry_id": "e4211b83-90f4-3bc7-a1d6-7a507d2bc35d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Thing, item (term that can be used to refer to any entity)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74d48d73-5935-4dcc-af85-f6157dfd2e5f",
                                                "sense_id": "03fc7a54-b72b-3bbf-bbbe-568d9f8581e2",
                                                "text": "This guy, here, controls the current, and this guy, here, measures the voltage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "10404cca-b3b8-4a5c-9c0d-b5438062b97d",
                                                "sense_id": "03fc7a54-b72b-3bbf-bbbe-568d9f8581e2",
                                                "text": "This guy is the partial derivative of that guy with respect to x."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "guy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b57c73b5-c643-3a75-b18a-5463c16710b1",
                                        "entry_id": "902e43b5-afdb-3300-80f8-171b1471fd4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To exhibit an effigy of Guy Fawkes around the 5th November."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a095197d-5aed-3fd0-a8d3-f14ef926fcce",
                                        "entry_id": "902e43b5-afdb-3300-80f8-171b1471fd4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make fun of, to ridicule with wit or innuendo."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd6de7e8-c792-4fc6-acd0-3f2f069a0212",
                                                "sense_id": "a095197d-5aed-3fd0-a8d3-f14ef926fcce",
                                                "text": "The dusky hunters \"guyed\" the palefaces who could not do as well as they with their primitive weapons, even though the fire spouted from the iron tubes and the balls that could not be seen by the eye carried death farther than did the missiles launched by the natives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8db2b075-db1f-476d-ba78-e7ff2570e524",
                                                "sense_id": "a095197d-5aed-3fd0-a8d3-f14ef926fcce",
                                                "text": "Swift and other satirists mercilessly guyed the unlettered self-importance of the peddlars of such soul-food, exposing their humility and self-laceration as an egregious and obnoxious form of self-advertisement (s'excuser, c'est s'accuser)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b654252-5e37-44e2-ba03-d8abe38d1909",
                                                "sense_id": "a095197d-5aed-3fd0-a8d3-f14ef926fcce",
                                                "text": "Terry Kilmartin [...], applauded for every ‘um’ and ‘ah’, knew that he was being guyed and had the charm to make it funny."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa775c87-3656-3944-a5a9-a7a85ea46efe",
                                        "entry_id": "902e43b5-afdb-3300-80f8-171b1471fd4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To play in a comedic manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "169bc056-950c-45f1-b4ab-187373a51f56",
                                                "sense_id": "aa775c87-3656-3944-a5a9-a7a85ea46efe",
                                                "text": "To guy the speech in the manner of an old-fashioned 'ham' for cheap laughs...."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
